# Code Standards

## TL;DR

{{3–5 lines an agent can stop at: the facts that change what it does next.}}

## Language & types

- {{TypeScript strict; no `any` without a written justification}}
- {{Two-space indentation}}
- {{Naming: components PascalCase, files kebab-case, hooks use-*}}

## Implementation conventions

Installed versions come from manifests/lockfiles; version-specific usage belongs in [library notes](library-docs.md). Keep only coding conventions here.

- {{e.g. Server Components by default; "use client" only where interactivity requires}}
- {{e.g. Server actions pattern for mutations; no separate API layer for form submits}}
- {{e.g. Route protection lives in proxy/middleware — check library-docs.md, this moved between versions}}

## Structure

- {{Where API handlers live, where schemas live, where agents live, etc.}}
- {{Component structure: one exported component per file unless trivial}}

## Error handling

- {{e.g. Never swallow errors; log with the project logger; user-facing errors carry an actionable message}}
- {{e.g. Every try/catch either fixes, retries, or re-throws — no empty catches}}

## Verification references

Use [testing.md](testing.md) for declared commands, test conventions and evidence. Follow [workflow-rules.md](workflow-rules.md) for verification/review procedure; do not maintain another command list or completion gate here.
